From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: FT: defer the PTK until association

hostapd patch 896, now Giuseppe Piscitelli's "ft: defer PTK installation
for unassociated AP clients" (hostap list 2026-10-18), which openwrt#26652
carries since 2026-11-14 in place of our own patch (hostap list
2026-11-04). B137: at FT authentication wpa_ft_install_ptk() tried to
configure the PTK before the STA is associated; mac80211 refuses a
pairwise key for an STA that is not associated yet (-ENOENT), so every
FT roam logged

  nl80211: kernel reports: key addition failed

at daemon.err, and the PTK was configured after association anyway by
the WPA_ASSOC_FT retry. Our patch skipped that early attempt except
after the PMF re-add of a station that still had an association; his
covers that case too.

W-118 PMF bench 2026-11-14 (two separate hostapd processes as two APs,
ieee80211w=2, QCA9882 station roaming A -> B -> A): our patch 8/8 roams
with 7 errors on the 7 re-add returns, his 8/8 roams with none, the
station's CCMP key in place and carrying data after the last re-add.

Bump PKG_RELEASE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile     |  2 +-
 ...nassociated-AP-clients.patch | 88 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 89 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile b/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
index 608ccdfbe88439af0ef078b11c10b3c0b938d423..0876c431af53b0f47ef0523804954f27a4ff8ad3 100644
--- a/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
+++ b/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=hostapd
-PKG_RELEASE:=17
+PKG_RELEASE:=18
 
 PKG_SOURCE_URL:=https://w1.fi/hostap.git
 PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
diff --git a/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/896-ft-defer-PTK-installation-for-unassociated-AP-clients.patch b/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/896-ft-defer-PTK-installation-for-unassociated-AP-clients.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..24d3dc58a4a524d530321c3b8e818c4e5cf823a0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/896-ft-defer-PTK-installation-for-unassociated-AP-clients.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,88 @@
+From 72f47b0a1e8f4fd96d6965ae7ea20e3a4de84637 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Giuseppe Piscitelli <ooonea@gmail.com>
+Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 05:07:10 -0700
+Subject: [PATCH] ft: defer PTK installation for unassociated AP clients
+
+mac80211 rejects an ordinary FT PTK before the driver station is
+associated. hostapd retries after association, but the early request
+produces a key-add error for each transition.
+
+Honor the FT station preparation callback before installing the PTK.
+For drivers exposing full AP client state, defer ordinary FT keys until
+association. Preserve PMF station cleanup and early installation for EPP
+peers, which need the key for encrypted association frames. Keep early
+installation when the callback is absent.
+
+Tested eight hwsim FT-SAE roams with required PMF, including OTA and
+over-DS, with bidirectional traffic after every roam. Key-add errors
+changed from eight to zero. A backport on OpenWrt 25.12.6 with ath11k
+also completed a real FT roam with PMF and bidirectional traffic,
+without the key-add error observed with the original build.
+
+Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Piscitelli <ooonea@gmail.com>
+Assisted-by: OpenAI Codex
+Link: https://patchwork.ozlabs.org/project/hostap/patch/CACmoRBbY__xZOxYfpi0Mo+ErCxk_PsJcfQfjq+7RNeKgObYH-A@mail.gmail.com/
+---
+ src/ap/wpa_auth.h      |  1 +
+ src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c   | 13 +++----------
+ src/ap/wpa_auth_glue.c |  8 +++++++-
+ 3 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)
+
+--- a/src/ap/wpa_auth.h
++++ b/src/ap/wpa_auth.h
+@@ -419,6 +419,7 @@ struct wpa_auth_callbacks {
+ 				   const u8 *eapol, size_t eapol_len);
+ #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211R_AP
+ 	struct wpa_state_machine * (*add_sta)(void *ctx, const u8 *sta_addr);
++	/* Nonzero defers PTK installation until the post-association retry. */
+ 	int (*add_sta_ft)(void *ctx, const u8 *sta_addr);
+ 	int (*set_vlan)(void *ctx, const u8 *sta_addr,
+ 			struct vlan_description *vlan);
+--- a/src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c
++++ b/src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c
+@@ -2869,7 +2869,7 @@ static inline int wpa_auth_add_sta_ft(st
+ 				      const u8 *addr)
+ {
+ 	if (!wpa_auth->cb->add_sta_ft)
+-		return -1;
++		return 0;
+ 	return wpa_auth->cb->add_sta_ft(wpa_auth->cb_ctx, addr);
+ }
+ 
+@@ -2896,15 +2896,8 @@ void wpa_ft_install_ptk(struct wpa_state
+ 		return;
+ 	}
+ 
+-	if (!retry)
+-		wpa_auth_add_sta_ft(sm->wpa_auth, sm->addr);
+-
+-	/* FIX: add STA entry to kernel/driver here? The set_key will fail
+-	 * most likely without this.. At the moment, STA entry is added only
+-	 * after association has been completed. This function will be called
+-	 * again after association to get the PTK configured, but that could be
+-	 * optimized by adding the STA entry earlier.
+-	 */
++	if (!retry && wpa_auth_add_sta_ft(sm->wpa_auth, sm->addr))
++		return;
+ 	if (wpa_auth_set_key(sm->wpa_auth, 0, alg, sm->addr, sm->keyidx_active,
+ 			     sm->PTK.tk, klen, KEY_FLAG_PAIRWISE_RX_TX))
+ 		return;
+--- a/src/ap/wpa_auth_glue.c
++++ b/src/ap/wpa_auth_glue.c
+@@ -1335,9 +1335,15 @@ static int hostapd_wpa_auth_add_sta_ft(v
+ 		 * previous association. */
+ 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
+ 			   "FT: Remove and re-add driver STA entry after successful FT authentication");
+-		return ap_sta_re_add(hapd, sta);
++		if (ap_sta_re_add(hapd, sta))
++			return -1;
+ 	}
+ 
++	/* EPP needs the key before the encrypted association exchange. */
++	if (FULL_AP_CLIENT_STATE_SUPP(hapd->iface->drv_flags) &&
++	    !(sta->flags & WLAN_STA_ASSOC) && !ap_sta_is_epp(sta))
++		return 1;
++
+ 	return 0;
+ }
+ 
-- 
